  "query_preview": "any further in time given the confidence that the front\nshould push far enough south to not cause any more heavy showers\nbeyond the 8am EDT today. \n\n\nKEY MESSAGE 2...Temperatures at or below normal through the weekend.\n\nNortherly winds due to surface high pressure north of the region\ncombined with eastern conus troughing will lead to well below\nnormal temperatures for the next few days through Saturday.\nHighs will generally run in the low to mid 70s areawide, with\nlows falling into the low 60s to mid 60s areawide. \n\nOverall rain chances look to remain minimal over the next couple\nof days; however, an upper level shortwave moving through the\narea late Friday looks to lead to some mountain showers and\nthunderstorms Friday night into Saturday.",
